Tartarus Engine @PROJECT_VERSION@ (@TARTARUS_GIT_DESCRIBE@)
==========================================================

Windows x64. Unzip anywhere and run TartarusEngine.exe - there is no installer and nothing is
written to the registry. Everything the editor needs is in this folder.


WHAT IS IN HERE
---------------
  TartarusEngine.exe        the editor
  TartarusEditor.dll        editor panels (hot-reloadable)
  TartarusGame.dll          gameplay systems (hot-reloadable)
  PhysX*.dll                NVIDIA PhysX 5 runtime
  assets/                   engine-owned content: shaders, fonts, branding, smoke-test scenes
  project/                  the sample project the editor opens on first run
  LICENSE                   this engine's licence
  THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md    licences of everything it is built on

Your own settings (preferences, shortcuts, panel layout, logs) do NOT live here. They go to
%LOCALAPPDATA%\TartarusEngine\ so this folder stays disposable - delete it, unzip a newer
build, and your setup carries over.


THE SAMPLE PROJECT IS MISSING TWO SETS OF FILES
-----------------------------------------------
The Sandbox scene opens on first run, and two kinds of asset it uses cannot be redistributed
in this download:

  * Characters and animations (project/assets/characters/)
    Mixamo's licence does not allow redistributing the FBX files. Download "Y Bot" and the
    "Male Locomotion Pack" from mixamo.com into project/assets/characters/ybot/.

  * Sky HDRIs (project/assets/sky/)
    CC0 from Poly Haven, but too large to ship here. The scene names the file it wants
    (see "skyHdriPath" in project/scenes/Sandbox.json); download it from polyhaven.com
    into project/assets/sky/.

The scene loads without them. The Console will warn about each missing asset, the characters
will not appear, and the sky falls back to a procedural gradient. Everything else - the arena,
physics, the gravity gun, lighting and post-processing - works as shipped.


IF IT WILL NOT START
--------------------
The engine needs a real OpenGL 4.6 core context with compute shader support. If it exits with
a message about the OpenGL version, update your GPU driver; Intel/AMD/NVIDIA drivers from the
last few years all supply 4.6. Remote Desktop sessions and some VMs expose only a software
adapter below 4.6 and will not run it.

Crash dumps, if any, land next to the executable as crash_<pid>_<timestamp>.dmp with a .txt
summary beside them. Both are useful in a bug report, along with Preferences > About >
Copy report.
